.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# --- Private: this board's own reads and readbacks ---------------------------
# Full 16 MiB reads carry the board's real GbE MAC address and live ME/NVRAM
# state (docs/BUILD_AND_PORTING.md, "Board identity"). Never publish them.
backups/*
!backups/README.md

# --- Generated: build output ---------------------------------------------------
# Regenerable from source + your reads, and built from a private read, so it
# carries the same board identity as backups/.
build/

# --- Historical images ---------------------------------------------------------
# Every historical .bin was built from either this board's reads (private) or
# HP's image (not ours to redistribute). The evidence sidecars that were already
# tracked stay tracked; the rest of the folder is local-only.
research/images/*
!research/images/README.md
!research/images/ref-platform-modules-without-tpm2-core.bin.report.txt
!research/images/ref-first-tpm2-core-candidate.bin.json
!research/images/ref-first-tpm2-core-candidate.bin.report.txt
!research/images/ref-gnu-ld-candidate.bin.json
!research/images/board-gnu-ld-candidate-no-post.bin.json
!research/images/board-lld-unrebased-pei-hang.bin.json

# --- Third-party vendor material: re-obtain, never commit ---------------------
# HP SoftPaq SP103785, the Supermicro donor BIOS and UEFIExtract live here.
# docs/SETUP.md has exact hashes and official sources.
vendor-cache/*
!vendor-cache/README.md

# Infineon's TPM firmware updater + firmware image (tools/tpm_firmware_update/):
# keep our own README/scripts tracked, not Infineon's binaries/firmware/PDF.
tools/tpm_firmware_update/*.efi
tools/tpm_firmware_update/*.exe
tools/tpm_firmware_update/*.sys
tools/tpm_firmware_update/*.BIN
tools/tpm_firmware_update/*.pdf
tools/tpm_firmware_update/Infineon_Package_Readme.txt
tools/tpm_firmware_update/*.zip
